{"agent_id":"pp3g-91s9-web-research-task-issue-147-before-filing-an-upstream","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:23:20.472945512Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"96e2152d-85c5-465e-b90f-2d593b463473","comment_uuid":"aae87853-bc97-4cea-9ca7-7329671bb87c","author":"pp3g-91s9-web-research-task-issue-147-before-filing-an-upstream","content":"Verdict (web research, 2026-08-03): #145 is a DUPLICATE at the root-cause/behavior level, not novel. The closest exact upstream report is https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/39516 (draft, Jul 29): explicitly says chunkTimeout wrapped only text/event-stream and proposes wrapping every streamed response body; linked issue #31122 (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/31122) reports the resulting LLM stream deadlock. Earlier direct report https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/26487 (May 9) documents the same guard in wrapSSE returning raw non-SSE responses, with Bedrock application/vnd.amazon.eventstream bypassing chunkTimeout; proposed remove the content-type guard or expand matching. Related proposed fix https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/35743 (Jul 7) adds eventstream matching and per-provider content-type allowlisting, but is still open. These are the reports to reference when filing, especially #39516 and #26487; #145's stronger finding (any non-text/event-stream response can hang indefinitely with no error while RUNNING) is a new reproduction/impact framing, not a new underlying bug. Other relevant reports: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/39968 (Jul 31) says chunkTimeout only watches raw bytes, misses parsed-stream stalls, and a half-open stream lasted 9.5h; https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/37580 reports silently dropped SSE streams hanging sessions/subagents; https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/36739 reports opencode serve wedging on a hanging upstream SSE endpoint; https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/40205 (Aug 3, v1.18.11) reports opencode-go streaming freezes with no error/log recovery; https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/40065 reports opencode-go empty response/hang in v1.18.11. Search of Reddit r/LocalLLaMA was blocked (403), and HN search was JS-only; no independently verifiable Reddit/HN/Discord/blog URL was found in this quick pass. Workarounds evidenced by upstream material: use a finite overall provider timeout (the #26487 report notes it is the only remaining protection), prefer a provider/content type that emits SSE, or apply/test the approach in draft #39516 (wrap all response bodies) / #35743 (include eventstream). External watchdog/manual abort remains necessary when timeout is disabled or the stream stalls above the raw-byte layer. Recommendation: file upstream as a follow-up/variant referencing #39516, #26487, and #35743, clearly distinguishing the arbitrary non-SSE response case and zero-error RUNNING symptom.","created_at":"2026-08-03T18:23:20.465508293Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:n8URn1lTQac8RA1TDZi0xDrRKBTeEpi1MlWckqppfdQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoYFGC2LAgR+K+aZ/NudHdCZBHdzR9vkQBa9Iaav7uswAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA8d9KTKkSBj0vabBqfjWOHO1mKS+6huu6zl3G8dQ9ZOSocY6NrKN5I7vslA5NztZiu3SF6guJzjaeiJIWs62CDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:n8URn1lTQac8RA1TDZi0xDrRKBTeEpi1MlWckqppfdQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoYFGC2LAgR+K+aZ/NudHdCZBHdzR9vkQBa9Iaav7uswAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP6fV34r86Poe8+YF5v62X8VgwhktC1aRW42mnVE14emeU3Qr2Psvl6kgnkNPlHVrmI3PsJYRGPG8tT6OnPydgw="}
